That is the one real difference between them, and it matters
when the program uses the counter afterwards. If it does, the while version is what you want;
if it does not, the for keeps things tidy.

Read the constraint before you choose the tool. Where nothing is forbidden,
<code>StringBuilder</code> in a loop is the better answer and the 2024/2025 solution uses it;
where the paper bans it, using it costs the marks whatever the output.
